{"alias":"/safety/emergencymanagement","title":"School Emergency Management","changed":"2026-08-21T10:33:22+00:00","before":"<div class=\"blockhead\">\r\n<h2>School Emergency Management</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p>The Maine School Safety Center (MSSC) will provide school emergency management training for all our interested parties and constituents. Our training will consist of a basic, intermediate, and advanced training.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-4 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Partners</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.fema.gov/\">FEMA</a> - Federal Emergency Management Agency</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/mema/\">MEMA</a> - Maine Emergency Management Agency</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/\">CISA</a> - Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-8 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Required FEMA Courses for School Administrators</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://training.fema.gov/is/courseoverview.aspx?code=IS-100.c&amp;lang=en\">ICS 100C</a> - Introduction to the Incident Command System</li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://training.fema.gov/is/courseoverview.aspx?code=IS-200.c&amp;lang=en\">ICS 200C</a> - Basic Incident Command for Initial Response</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://training.fema.gov/is/courseoverview.aspx?code=IS-700.b&amp;lang=en\">ICS 700B</a> - An Introduction to the National Incident Management System</li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://training.fema.gov/is/courseoverview.aspx?code=IS-800.d&amp;lang=en\">ICS 800D</a> - National Response Framework: An Introduction</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\">\r\n<h2>Maine Requirements</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Maine DOE Rules</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/statutes/20-A/title20-Asec1001.html\">School Board approval of the Comprehensive Health and Safety Emergency Management Plan</a> (Section 16)</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\">Lockdown and Evacuation Drills: link coming soon</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Bomb Threat Reporting &amp; Laws</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<p><a href=\"https://neo.maine.gov/DOE/NEO/Accounts/Account/Login\">Mandatory Online Bomb Threat Reporting</a> - The Maine Department of Education's secure school bomb threat reporting database requires administrators to have a username and a case-sensitive password to report incidents. Your local Superintendent Office should have the username and password on file.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h4>Related Laws</h4>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"http://www.mainelegislature.org/legis/statutes/20-a/title20-Asec263.html\">Response to school bomb threats, Section 263</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"http://www.mainelegislature.org/legis/statutes/20-a/title20-asec1001.html\">School bomb threat response policies, Section 1001.17</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"http://www.mainelegislature.org/legis/statutes/20-a/title20-asec1001.html\">Bomb threat information in student handbooks, Section 1001.18</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\">\r\n<h2>Emergency Operations Planning (EOP)</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p>The MSSC will provide training, guidance, and ongoing support to schools in order to assure every school in Maine possesses a comprehensive, high-quality school emergency operations plan.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"dc-note\">\r\n<p><em>Organizations and resources included are for reference and information only; they are not an endorsement from the Maine Department of Education.</em></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Guidance</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20CISA%20Security%20Planning%20Workbook%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">CISA Security Planning Workbook</a> - Aids in EOP development</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Guide%20for%20Developing%20Emergency%20Operations%20Plans%20Checklist%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Checklist for Developing High-Quality EOPs</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Developing%20and%20Maintaining%20Emergency%20Operation%20Plans%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Guide for Developing&nbsp;and Maintaining EOPs</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20FEMA%20Sample%20Plan%20-%209.8.2025.pdf\">FEMA Sample Plan</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Threat%20and%20Hazard%20Identification%20and%20Risk%20Assessment%20%28THIRA%29%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Threat and Hazard Identification and Risk Assessment (THIRA)</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.ready.gov/kids\">Ready Kids</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://iloveuguys.org/The-Standard-Response-Protocol.html\">Standard Response Protocol</a> (I Love U Guys Foundation)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Exercises</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/services/cisa-tabletop-exercise-packages\">CISA Tabletop Exercises</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://preptoolkit.fema.gov/web/em-toolkits\">FEMA Tabletop Exercises</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Emergency%20Exercises%20Fact%20Sheet%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Emergency Exercises Fact Sheet</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Resources</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h4>Former REMS TA</h4>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Guide%20for%20Developing%20High-Quality%20Emergency%20Operation%20Plans%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Developing Emergency Operation Plans Checklists</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Site%20Assessments%20Protocols%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Site Assessments Protocol</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Emergency%20Exercises%20Fact%20Sheet%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Emergency Exercises Fact Sheet</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20CybersecurityTabletop%20-%209.9.2025.pdf\">Cybersecurity Tabletop</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20K12%20Cybersecurity%20Fact%20Sheet%20-%209.9.2025.pdf\">K-12 Cybersecurity Fact Sheet</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h4>CISA</h4>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/k-12-school-security-guide\">K-12 School Security Guide Suite</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/2023-12/Social%20Media%20Threat%20Guidance%20for%20School%20Staff%20and%20Authorities%20Infographic_508.pdf\">Social Media Threat Guidance</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Handouts</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Planning%20Principles.pdf\">Safety Team Planning Principles</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Identifying%20Core%20Planning%20Teams%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Identifying Core Planning Teams</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20safety%20-%20Emergency%20Operations%20Considerations%20for%20Athletic%20Directors%20-%203.20.2025.pdf\">Emergency Operations Considerations for Athletic Directors</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a class=\"file file--mime-application-pdf file--application-pdf\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"2000dcd6-a4b6-40f4-8d58-19592a4764f0\" filename=\"School Safety - Ten Safety Priorities - 8.19.2026.pdf\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Ten%20Safety%20Priorities%20-%208.19.2026.pdf\">Back to School 10 Safety Priorities</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\">\r\n<h2>Grant Opportunities</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Funding Sources</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.schoolsafety.gov/grants-finder-tool\">SchoolSafety.gov Grants Finder Tool</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.greenlightsgrantinitiative.org/\">Greenlights Grant Initiative</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://cops.usdoj.gov/grants\">DOJ COPS Grants</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/mema/grants\">MEMA Grants</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://bja.ojp.gov/taxonomy/term/school-resource-officers-sro\">BJA School Resource Officer Grants</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://grantfinder.com/\">Grant Finder</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"contact-cube\">\r\n<h3><strong>Contact</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Jack Peck</strong><br />\r\n<em>School Emergency Management Coordinator</em><br />\r\n<strong>Email:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:Jack.Peck@maine.gov\">Jack.Peck@maine.gov</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n","after":"<div class=\"doe-hero\">\n<p class=\"doe-eyebrow\">Maine School Safety Center Services</p>\n<p class=\"doe-contact-link\"><a href=\"#contact\">Contact</a></p>\n<p class=\"doe-lead\">The Maine School Safety Center (MSSC) will provide school emergency management training for all our interested parties and constituents. Our training will consist of a basic, intermediate, and advanced training.</p>\n<nav class=\"doe-toc\"><h3>On this page</h3><ol><li><a href=\"#maine-requirements\">Maine Requirements</a></li><li><a href=\"#emergency-operations-planning-eop\">Emergency Operations Planning (EOP)</a></li><li><a href=\"#grant-opportunities\">Grant Opportunities</a></li></ol></nav>\n</div>\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"doe-row--uneven doe-row--stack row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-4 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Partners</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-item list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.fema.gov/\">FEMA</a>  Federal Emergency Management Agency</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-item list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/mema/\">MEMA</a>  Maine Emergency Management Agency</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-item list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/\">CISA</a>  Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-8 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Required FEMA Courses for School Administrators</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-item\"><a href=\"https://training.fema.gov/is/courseoverview.aspx?code=IS-100.c&amp;lang=en\">ICS 100C</a>  Introduction to the Incident Command System</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-item\"><a href=\"https://training.fema.gov/is/courseoverview.aspx?code=IS-200.c&amp;lang=en\">ICS 200C</a>  Basic Incident Command for Initial Response</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-item\"><a href=\"https://training.fema.gov/is/courseoverview.aspx?code=IS-700.b&amp;lang=en\">ICS 700B</a>  An Introduction to the National Incident Management System</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-item\"><a href=\"https://training.fema.gov/is/courseoverview.aspx?code=IS-800.d&amp;lang=en\">ICS 800D</a>  National Response Framework: An Introduction</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\" id=\"maine-requirements\">\r\n<h2>Maine Requirements</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"doe-row--uneven doe-row--stack row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-4 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Maine DOE Rules</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/statutes/20-A/title20-Asec1001.html\">School Board approval of the Comprehensive Health and Safety Emergency Management Plan</a> (Section 16)</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item\">Lockdown and Evacuation Drills: link coming soon</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-8 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Bomb Threat Reporting &amp; Laws</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<p><a href=\"https://neo.maine.gov/DOE/NEO/Accounts/Account/Login\">Mandatory Online Bomb Threat Reporting</a> - The Maine Department of Education's secure school bomb threat reporting database requires administrators to have a username and a case-sensitive password to report incidents. Your local Superintendent Office should have the username and password on file.</p>\r\n<h3>Related Laws</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"http://www.mainelegislature.org/legis/statutes/20-a/title20-Asec263.html\">Response to school bomb threats, Section 263</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"http://www.mainelegislature.org/legis/statutes/20-a/title20-asec1001.html\">School bomb threat response policies, Section 1001.17</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"http://www.mainelegislature.org/legis/statutes/20-a/title20-asec1001.html\">Bomb threat information in student handbooks, Section 1001.18</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\" id=\"emergency-operations-planning-eop\">\r\n<h2>Emergency Operations Planning (EOP)</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p>The MSSC will provide training, guidance, and ongoing support to schools in order to assure every school in Maine possesses a comprehensive, high-quality school emergency operations plan.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"dc-note\">\r\n<p><em>Organizations and resources included are for reference and information only; they are not an endorsement from the Maine Department of Education.</em></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"doe-row--uneven doe-row--stack row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-8 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Guidance</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-item list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20CISA%20Security%20Planning%20Workbook%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">CISA Security Planning Workbook</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span> Aids in EOP development</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Guide%20for%20Developing%20Emergency%20Operations%20Plans%20Checklist%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Checklist for Developing High-Quality EOPs</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Developing%20and%20Maintaining%20Emergency%20Operation%20Plans%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Guide for Developing&nbsp;and Maintaining EOPs</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20FEMA%20Sample%20Plan%20-%209.8.2025.pdf\">FEMA Sample Plan</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Threat%20and%20Hazard%20Identification%20and%20Risk%20Assessment%20%28THIRA%29%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Threat and Hazard Identification and Risk Assessment (THIRA)</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.ready.gov/kids\">Ready Kids</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://iloveuguys.org/The-Standard-Response-Protocol.html\">Standard Response Protocol</a> (I Love U Guys Foundation)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-4 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Exercises</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/services/cisa-tabletop-exercise-packages\">CISA Tabletop Exercises</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://preptoolkit.fema.gov/web/em-toolkits\">FEMA Tabletop Exercises</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Emergency%20Exercises%20Fact%20Sheet%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Emergency Exercises Fact Sheet</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Resources</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h3>Former REMS TA</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Guide%20for%20Developing%20High-Quality%20Emergency%20Operation%20Plans%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Developing Emergency Operation Plans Checklists</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Site%20Assessments%20Protocols%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Site Assessments Protocol</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Emergency%20Exercises%20Fact%20Sheet%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Emergency Exercises Fact Sheet</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20CybersecurityTabletop%20-%209.9.2025.pdf\">Cybersecurity Tabletop</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20K12%20Cybersecurity%20Fact%20Sheet%20-%209.9.2025.pdf\">K-12 Cybersecurity Fact Sheet</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>CISA</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/k-12-school-security-guide\">K-12 School Security Guide Suite</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/2023-12/Social%20Media%20Threat%20Guidance%20for%20School%20Staff%20and%20Authorities%20Infographic_508.pdf\">Social Media Threat Guidance</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6 py-2\">\r\n<div class=\"card h-100\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Handouts</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Planning%20Principles.pdf\">Safety Team Planning Principles</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Identifying%20Core%20Planning%20Teams%20-%209.4.2025.pdf\">Identifying Core Planning Teams</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20safety%20-%20Emergency%20Operations%20Considerations%20for%20Athletic%20Directors%20-%203.20.2025.pdf\">Emergency Operations Considerations for Athletic Directors</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Safety%20-%20Ten%20Safety%20Priorities%20-%208.19.2026.pdf\">Back to School 10 Safety Priorities</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">PDF</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blockhead\" id=\"grant-opportunities\">\r\n<h2>Grant Opportunities</h2>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Funding Sources</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.schoolsafety.gov/grants-finder-tool\">SchoolSafety.gov Grants Finder Tool</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.greenlightsgrantinitiative.org/\">Greenlights Grant Initiative</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://cops.usdoj.gov/grants\">DOJ COPS Grants</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/mema/grants\">MEMA Grants</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://bja.ojp.gov/taxonomy/term/school-resource-officers-sro\">BJA School Resource Officer Grants</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item\"><a href=\"https://grantfinder.com/\">Grant Finder</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"contact\" class=\"contact-cube\">\r\n<h3>Contact</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Jack Peck</strong><br />\r\n<em>School Emergency Management Coordinator</em><br />\r\n<strong>Email:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:Jack.Peck@maine.gov\">Jack.Peck@maine.gov</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\n<p class=\"doe-jump\"><a href=\"#contact\">Contact</a></p>\n<p class=\"doe-top\"><a href=\"#top\">Back to top</a></p>","notes":[],"decisions":[{"id":"filechip","on":true,"label":"Tag a document link with the format it opens","why":"16 links on this page open a file — 16 PDF — and say nothing about it, while others in the same list carry a tag because their author typed one. The format is read from the file name, so the list stops being half-labelled. No link text changes.","value":"16 links"},{"id":"uneven","on":true,"label":"Let very uneven cards find their own height","why":"3 rows pair a short card with one holding nearly three times as much. Equal heights stretch the short one and the difference reads as a hole, so these are allowed to sit at the height of what is in them.","value":"3 rows"},{"id":"balance","on":true,"label":"Give the cards the width their content needs","why":"2 rows hold two cards of very different weight in equal halves, and cards in a row are the same height — so the short one is stretched and the difference shows as empty space. 3.4× — 309 characters beside 91. Only the column widths change.","value":"2 rows"},{"id":"itemdash","on":true,"label":"Drop the dash once the link is set apart","why":"8 of those items separate the link from its description with a dash. The link is now set in the display face at a larger size with a chevron after it, so the dash marks a boundary that is already unmistakable. Only the separator is removed — no word changes.","value":"8 separators"},{"id":"items","on":true,"label":"Separate a link from its description","why":"8 list items open with a link and then explain it, all at the same weight — so the thing you can click is no easier to find than the sentence about it. The link becomes the item and the explanation sits under it.","value":"8 items"},{"id":"echo","on":true,"label":"Remove the first section header","removes":"School Emergency Management","why":"\"School Emergency Management\" repeats the page title, so the reader is told the same thing twice before any content."},{"id":"deck","on":true,"label":"Use this paragraph as the page description","why":"It is the page’s own opening paragraph, moved into the banner rather than rewritten.","value":"The Maine School Safety Center (MSSC) will provide school emergency management training for all our interested parties and constituents. Our training will consist of a basic, intermediate, and advanced training."},{"id":"capheadings","on":true,"label":"Bring every heading up to h3 or above","why":"3 headings sat at h4 or deeper inside a card, a callout, a contact block or an accordion panel — components the outline walk leaves alone because they label a thing rather than a section. A reader using a screen reader still hears the level, so a fourth-level title inside a page that only goes to three is announced as belonging to a level that does not exist. Each is styled by its class and its position rather than its number, so nothing changes on screen.","value":"3 headings"},{"id":"toc","on":true,"label":"Add a contents list (3 sections)","why":"Built from the section headings already on the page. Below three sections a list is not a route."},{"id":"eyebrow","on":true,"label":"Eyebrow: \"Maine School Safety Center Services\"","why":"Taken from the parent page, /safety."}],"mechanical":["empty paragraphs removed: 1","drupal entity attrs stripped: 4","loose text wrapped in a paragraph: 9","redundant bold inside a heading removed: 1","paragraph unwrapped inside a card header: 9","manual rules above headings removed: 1","action links marked: 30"],"findings":[],"safe":true,"audit":{"alias":"/safety/emergencymanagement","title":"School Emergency Management","changed":"2026-08-21T10:33:22+00:00","words":383,"bytes":10470,"fixes":["empty paragraphs removed: 1","drupal entity at